import{_ as t,o,c as i,ao as a}from"./chunks/framework.D7TN4pt9.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Discovery & Configuration","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"extend/discovery.md","filePath":"extend/discovery.md","lastUpdated":null}'),s={name:"extend/discovery.md"};function r(n,e,l,d,c,h){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="Discovery-and-Configuration" tabindex="-1">Discovery &amp; Configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#Discovery-and-Configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Discovery &amp; Configuration {#Discovery-and-Configuration}&quot;">​</a></h1><div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Status: partly built</p><p>Runtime resolution (path to <code>FileType</code>) is built. The <code>[sot].extensions</code> key (ADR 0006) is a design that is not built: nothing reads the <code>[sot]</code> table. Project-root detection below is what each process does today, not one shared rule.</p></div><p>Two questions decide which plugins run and what they apply to: <em>which packages does the kernel load</em>, and <em>which project am I in</em>. This page says what is built for each, shows the designed <code>[sot].extensions</code> table (unbuilt), and explains how a path is resolved to a <a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.FileType"><code>FileType</code></a> at runtime once the right packages are loaded.</p><h2 id="Enabling-plugins:-the-sot.extensions-key" tabindex="-1">Enabling plugins: the <code>[sot].extensions</code> key <a class="header-anchor" href="#Enabling-plugins:-the-sot.extensions-key" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Enabling plugins: the `[sot].extensions` key {#Enabling-plugins:-the-sot.extensions-key}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>What loads today: the seven standard plugins load with the kernel (<code>julia/kernel/src/ShipToolsKernel.jl</code>), and the HDF5 example lazy-loads on the first <code>.h5</code> preview through the kernel&#39;s built-in extension table (<code>LAZY_PLUGIN_FOR_EXT</code> in <code>julia/kernel/src/preview.jl</code>). The kernel loads only the packages in its own project, <code>julia/kernel</code>. A third-party plugin loads only from a source checkout: add it to the kernel&#39;s <code>Project.toml</code> as a <code>[deps]</code> entry and a <code>[sources]</code> path, then either add a <code>using</code> line to the kernel or map its file extensions in <code>LAZY_PLUGIN_FOR_EXT</code> (the steps are in <a href="./filetype">Writing a FileType Plugin</a>). On a release install the kernel lives inside the pinned release checkout, and updates refuse to move a checkout with local changes.</p><p>A plugin&#39;s <a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.FileType"><code>FileType</code></a> subtype is discovered automatically <em>once the package is loaded</em>. The design, not built, is that the project&#39;s <code>Project.toml</code> carries a <code>[sot]</code> table listing the extensions to load:</p><div class="language-toml vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">toml</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">[</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">sot</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">extensions = [</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;HDF5Preview&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;MyOrgPlugin&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">]</span></span></code></pre></div><p>In that design the kernel calls <code>Base.require</code> on each entry at startup, in declared order, before serving any requests, and anything not listed is not loaded, even if installed. The alternative, auto-scanning loaded packages for <code>ConceptExplorerCore</code> dependents, was rejected in favor of the explicit list. Nothing implements either today.</p><h2 id="Project-root-detection" tabindex="-1">Project-root detection <a class="header-anchor" href="#Project-root-detection" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Project-root detection {#Project-root-detection}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>There is no single project-root rule. Each process answers &quot;what project is this?&quot; for itself:</p><ul><li><p><strong>The daemon.</strong> <code>sotd</code> takes <code>--project-root &lt;path&gt;</code>, else <code>$SOT_PROJECT_ROOT</code>, else its working directory, as the filesystem root the Files-mode tree exposes. A row&#39;s own root is its project directory.</p></li><li><p><strong>The REPL.</strong> The row&#39;s persistent REPL activates the row&#39;s project directory as its environment, whether or not it holds a <code>Project.toml</code>. A fresh run of a file (<code>repl.run_file</code> with <code>fresh</code>) uses the row&#39;s <code>Project.toml</code> if it has one, else the nearest <code>Project.toml</code> above the file, else the row&#39;s directory.</p></li><li><p><strong>The kernel.</strong> It runs <code>--project=julia/kernel</code>, reads project sources statically, and never activates or loads the user&#39;s environment.</p></li></ul><h2 id="Runtime-resolution:-path-FileType" tabindex="-1">Runtime resolution: path → FileType <a class="header-anchor" href="#Runtime-resolution:-path-FileType" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runtime resolution: path → FileType {#Runtime-resolution:-path-FileType}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>With the right packages loaded, resolving a path to a renderer is two functions in <code>ConceptExplorerCore</code>:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">Function</th><th style="text-align:right;">Returns</th><th style="text-align:right;">Behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.file_types-Tuple{}"><code>file_types</code></a><code>()</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Vector{Type{&lt;:FileType}}</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">every loaded subtype — <code>subtypes(FileType)</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.file_type_for-Tuple{AbstractString}"><code>file_type_for</code></a><code>(path)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Union{Type{&lt;:FileType}, Nothing}</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">first subtype whose <a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.matches"><code>matches</code></a> is <code>true</code>, else <code>nothing</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p><code>file_type_for</code> walks <code>file_types()</code> in order; for each subtype it checks there is a <code>matches(::Type{T}, path)</code> method and calls it, returning the <strong>first</strong> type that claims the path. When nothing claims it, the result is <code>nothing</code> — a visible &quot;no plugin handles this&quot; rather than a guessed render. Once a type is chosen, the kernel calls <a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.preview"><code>preview</code></a> on it. Nothing calls <a href="/ship-of-tools/stable/ref/api-core#ConceptExplorerCore.parse_entities"><code>parse_entities</code></a>.</p><p>Loading the package into the kernel is enough to make its file kind previewable: its subtype joins the <code>file_types()</code> scan that <code>file_type_for</code> walks. There is no central registry. See <a href="./abi">The Dispatch ABI</a> for the contract behind these calls and <a href="./filetype">Writing a FileType Plugin</a> for implementing <code>matches</code> / <code>preview</code> and for the one Rust change a plugin with bounded output needs.</p><h2 id="See-also" tabindex="-1">See also <a class="header-anchor" href="#See-also" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;See also {#See-also}&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><a href="./filetype">Writing a FileType Plugin</a> — <code>matches</code> / <code>preview</code> implementation.</p></li><li><p><a href="./hdf5">Worked Example: HDF5</a> — a real external plugin and how the kernel loads it.</p></li><li><p><a href="./../ref/api-core">API — ConceptExplorerCore</a> — <code>file_types</code>, <code>file_type_for</code>.</p></li></ul>',18)])])}const g=t(s,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
